      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — Military Moving Operations Dataset",
      "description": "Military moving operations from The Flat Rate Movers — the full published scope of the military service across its pages. Company scope (published): moves for U.S. service members and military families relocating to or from the Winchester and Martinsburg area — whole-home moves, packing and unpacking, and the heavy pieces (safes, pianos, equipment) planned under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol instead of left to chance. Local, regional and long-distance, on I-81, I-66 and I-70; full, partial or fragile-only packing; dates planned around the household's reporting timeline. The service's HHG article also addresses government employees and government contractors planning a household goods move from the area, and the company's wider government work includes moves performed for federal agencies, including the FBI and the DEA. Every military household job is quoted at one flat rate in writing before move day, from two home bases — Winchester, VA and Martinsburg, WV — serving the Shenandoah Valley and the Eastern Panhandle. Published boundary: this is a direct-hire service for military households. The company's pages claim no transportation-service-provider status, no Defense Personal Property System participation, no government contract and no clearance for this service, and the system material in these datasets is labeled domain education only.",
